1. `async function getCameraAndMicrophoneStatus(callback)`
This method checks if the user has granted access to the camera and microphone and returns their current states as an object. If the user denies access, it does not attempt to open or close anything.

```javascript
const checkMediaAccess = async () => {
  try {
    const stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ video: true, audio: true });
    return { camera: stream.getVideoTracks().length > 0, microphone: stream.getAudioTracks().length > 0 };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error accessing media devices.', error);
    return { camera: false, microphone: false };
  }
};

async function getCameraAndMicrophoneStatus(callback) {
  const status = await checkMediaAccess();
  callback(status.camera, status.microphone);
}
```

2. `async function openCamera()`
This method opens the camera when it is closed and closes it when it is already open. It uses the MediaDevices API's `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia()` method to request access to the camera.

```javascript
let localStream;

async function openCamera() {
  try {
    localStream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ video: true, audio: false });
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Error opening camera.', err);
    return;
  }
}
```

