System.out.println("Total CO2 Emissions: " + totalCo2Emissions + " pounds");
```

2. Deforestation:
Deforestation disrupts the carbon cycle by removing trees that absorb CO2 during photosynthesis and releasing stored carbon when they decompose or burn. Additionally, deforested areas may become sources of CO2 if the land is converted to agricultural practices or livestock farming.

