```

Now, you can get the current user session by calling `firebase.auth().currentUser`. Here's an example:

```javascript
const firebaseConfig = {
  // Your Firebase config here
};

firebase.initializeApp(firebaseConfig);

const getSession = () => {
  firebase.auth().onAuthStateChanged((user) => {
    if (user) {
      const uid = user.uid;
      const email = user.email;
      console.log('User is signed in.', user);
      return user;
    } else {
      console.log('User is signed out.');
      return null;
    }
  });
};

getSession();
```

This example initializes Firebase and sets up an event listener for the authentication state change. When the user signs in or out, it logs a message and returns the corresponding user data.

